# Codejitsu AI — Operations

## Resource workflow

Create AI resources with `make:spark`, `make:vessel`, `make:skill`, `make:provider`, `make:tool`, and `make:toolset`. Inspect them with their corresponding `list` and `show` commands.

Run a Vessel once with `ai:run <vessel> <prompt>` or open its conversational interface with `ai:tui`. Tools are deny-by-default when consequential; one-shot execution can approve a named Tool with `--approve-tool=<name>`.

## Local models

`model://codejitsu/local` builds `codejitsu:latest` through Ollama from the cataloged Qwen2.5-Coder recipe.

- `model:list` lists Ollama models.
- `model:search <query>` searches Model Catalog entries.
- `model:show <name-or-uri>` shows a recipe and installed status.
- `model:build <name-or-uri>` builds directly.
- `model:ensure [name-or-uri]` interactively ensures availability and defaults to `codejitsu/local`.
- `model:test [name]` performs the response smoke test.

Weights belong under `var/models`; temporary rendered Modelfiles belong under `var/tmp/codejitsu-ai`; Ollama owns built layers.

## Memory guidance for Sparks

Load only Context relevant to the current task. Prefer package-local Context for package contracts and root `.context` for repository-wide state and decisions. Treat Context as durable guidance, then verify claims against current code, manifests, catalogs, and tests.
